# netsurf: navigator.getBattery() from the Vita's battery (patch 272)
# Generated 2026-10-13
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 271)
#
# The Battery Status API, backed by the hardware: frontends/vita
# js_platform.c macsurf_battery() reads scePowerGetBatteryLifePercent,
# scePowerIsBatteryCharging / IsPowerOnline and scePowerGetBatteryLifeTime
# (minutes left); the bridge's __vitaBattery() hands them to the
# polyfill's BatteryManager (an EventTarget): level, charging (or on
# external power), dischargingTime from the minutes left, chargingTime 0
# when full and Infinity otherwise (the Vita does not say). One manager
# per page, read again every minute, with levelchange / chargingchange /
# dischargingtimechange / chargingtimechange events and their on*
# handlers. The simulator's host reports no battery: the spec's defaults
# (charging, level 1, chargingTime 0, dischargingTime Infinity). Secure
# contexts only, as in Chromium.
#
# Gate: testpages/pages/JS-device-honest.html check 6 (DEVICE 6/6 with
# 271; Chromium 6/6). On the device: the level should match the Vita's
# own battery indicator.
